Google's API Discovery documents and the Google Workspace CLI (gws)

Discovery documents, https://developers.google.com/discovery
The machine-readable descriptions Google serves of its APIs, read on
2026-11-18 where gws reads them (www.googleapis.com/discovery/v1/apis/...,
or <api>.googleapis.com/$discovery/rest): Gmail, Calendar, Drive, Docs,
Sheets, Slides, Tasks, People, Chat, Classroom, Forms, Keep, Meet, Admin
reports, Workspace events, Model Armor, Apps Script and Search Console, each
at the revision and SHA-256 internal/controlplane/serviceproxy/
catalog_sources.json pins. The documents state no license of their own; they
are Google's, published for clients of its APIs.

What is taken from them here: of each method, its id, HTTP method, the host
and path a request to it has (the base URL and flatPath) and the paths its
media is uploaded to (internal/controlplane/serviceproxy/google_methods.json,
written by internal/controlplane/serviceproxy/catalogsgen). Nothing else of the
documents is kept. The catalog of actions made from that list is Hypomnema's
own (internal/controlplane/serviceproxy/google.go).

